                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2867: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-09T12:00:00-04:00">February 9,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Paraguay’s reply sent yesterday afternoon to the last note of the League read
                    in part as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Great as is our desire to reestablish peace we cannot lay down our arms
                            before an aggressor country which has invaded our territory with the
                            open design of conquest. This Government considers that to be
                            efficacious the exhortation should be directed especially to the country
                            which has provoked this cruel struggle and whose refusal to offer
                            adequate securities causes the conflict to continue.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
